  <h1 class="page-title">How to Redeem Sweeps Coins for Cash</h1>
  <div class="answer-first">
    <span class="af-label">Direct answer</span>
    <p>At operators that support cash prizes, request redemption from the account's redemption screen after you meet eligibility, identity-check, playthrough and minimum-balance requirements. Choose an available payment method, submit the request, and wait for operator approval and delivery. A displayed Sweeps Coins balance is not necessarily a redeemable balance.</p>
  </div>
  <p>This process is based on <a href="#process-source">YAY Casino's published redemption guide</a> and the dated operator records below. Screens, methods and conditions differ by operator. Entertainment-only coins are not cash prizes; gift cards and cryptocurrency are not the same as cash delivered to a bank account.</p>

  <h2 id="steps">Five steps to request a redemption</h2>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3">
    <li><strong>Check eligibility and product type.</strong> Read the operator's age, location and sweepstakes rules. The site's <a href="/availability/">state gate</a> is an offer policy, not legal clearance. Do not request cash from an entertainment-only product.</li>
    <li><strong>Complete identity verification.</strong> Follow the operator's secure verification flow. YAY's guide describes government ID, proof of address and a selfie check. Other operators can require different documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the redeemable balance.</strong> Confirm applicable playthrough and promotion conditions, then check the minimum for the specific method. Do not treat a gift-card minimum as a cash minimum.</li>
    <li><strong>Select a method and submit.</strong> Use the options actually offered in your account. Confirm the recipient details, amount and any disclosed fees before submitting. Keep the request confirmation.</li>
    <li><strong>Track review and delivery separately.</strong> An approved request may still be awaiting payment delivery. Check the stated processing window and contact operator support if the request exceeds it.</li>
  </ol>

